.TH KAGI-VOLUME-QEMU-SCSI 1 "November 2026" "Kagi 0.39.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kagi-volume-qemu-scsi \- print QEMU arguments for a Kagi-backed SCSI disk
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scripts/kagi-volume-qemu-scsi
.BR virtio-scsi | sas
.I HOST PORT
.RI [ DEVICE-ID ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints shell-escaped QEMU arguments for an NBD backend and a guest SCSI disk.
Use
.B virtio-scsi
for the paravirtualized PCI controller or
.B sas
for the emulated
.B mptsas1068
controller.
The disk ID defaults to
.BR keyspace0 .
.PP
Start the Kagi NBD frontend before starting QEMU.
Review the generated identifiers before combining the arguments with existing
devices.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kagi-volume-nbd (1),
.BR kagi-volume-libvirt-scsi (1),
.BR qemu-system-x86_64 (1)
